  "description": "The text describes a specific parenting mishap — realizing a son has taken the wrong backpack to school — which is visually represented by the woman’s exaggerated shocked expression. The visual material (shocked woman) is mapped onto the textual material (parenting mishap) to convey the emotional reaction to this common, relatable error. The woman’s distress is an exaggerated visual trope used to amplify the humor and absurdity of the situation described in the text.",
